BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AUDITIONS: A Peasant of El Salvador — Chandler Players
DTSTART:20261013T140000
DTEND:20261013T193000
DTSTAMP:20261012T202017Z
UID:4aba21f7d25da83df351ccc24de1bf@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The Chandler Players\, Chandler Center for the Arts’ communi
 ty theater group\, bring local performers together to tell stories onstage
  and welcome both new and experienced participants. The Chandler Players i
 nvite actors\, singers\, and community performers to audition for A Peasan
 t of El Salvador\, an acclaimed play by Vermont playwrights Peter Gould an
 d Stephen Stearns\, directed by Dominic Spillane. Performers of all ages\,
  backgrounds\, and experience levels are welcome. The production offers sp
 eaking and non-speaking roles\, along with a large ensemble participating 
 in group singing\, movement\, and storytelling. No prior stage experience 
 is required for ensemble participation. Performed around the world\, the p
 lay tells the powerful\, moving\, and often humorous story of a Salvadoran
  farmer and his family during political upheaval. Rooted in folk storytell
 ing\, it explores universal themes of family\, community\, resilience\, an
 d justice. The production will feature live music at every performance by 
 Grammy Award-winning composer Ernesto Villalobos. A portion of the proceed
 s will benefit Migrant Justice / Justicia Migrante. Performances will take
  place in March 2027 in Randolph and Winooski. Those unable to attend sche
 duled auditions can visit the Chandler Players page for video audition opt
 ions.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Chandler Center for the Arts\, 71 N. Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/auditions-
 a-peasant-of-el-salvador-chandler-players-03-10-2026-14-42-43
END:VEVENT
